# Every file in this repository is owned by the people listed here.
#
# Paired with "Require review from Code Owners" on `main`, this is what makes a
# LISTED person's approval specifically required — not just any approval.
#
# Without this file, branch protection only asks for "1 approving review", and
# GitHub lets ANY collaborator with write access give it. Six accounts besides
# the owner have write on this repo, so two of them could approve each other
# and merge to main without anyone here seeing the change. That is the thing
# this file prevents (2026-08-15).
#
# Adding a name here is a real grant: that person can approve and merge OTHER
# people's pull requests to production. It does NOT let them merge their own —
# GitHub does not accept a self-approval — so every change still passes a second
# pair of eyes.
#
# Keep this as a single catch-all line. Narrower per-directory rules would mean
# some paths quietly fall back to "any collaborator can approve".

